      "why": "The 100-eval sweep already found 71 feasible pipelined designs with best area 39973 um^2, and it owns the entire merged front. The throughput constraint (>=32 Msps) forces a 1-result/cycle architecture, which only pipelined/pipelined_m provide. The accuracy constraint (max_abs_err <= 2^-12) is met by n_iter>=12 with modest guards. The area objective pushes toward the minimum data_width and n_iter that still satisfy accuracy, so I focus the budget tightly on the 14-16 width / 12-14 iteration corner where the area-accuracy trade-off is sharpest. Keeping angle_guard and frac_guard in small ranges lets Optuna resolve the exact accuracy boundary and find the cheapest feasible point. This is the primary front-mapping effort."
