  "rationale": "The feasible Pareto front is well-established with 3 distinct designs covering the area-accuracy trade-off (37422-41349 um^2, 12.3-12.5 bits). All constraints are met by the front members: throughput (138-143 MSPS >= 32), max_abs_err (<= 0.000204 <= 0.000244), and sys_p99_batch_us (best seen 0.269 us <= 0.5 us). The selection rule (min area) clearly points to the pipelined design with data_width=17, n_iter=14, angle_guard=1, frac_guard=0, rounding=round at 37422 um^2. Further exploration would not improve the front significantly given the tight feasible region (data_width 16-17, n_iter 14-15) and the fact that pipelined_m yielded no feasible designs. The hypervolume gain of +135.1% in round 2 indicates strong convergence, and with no budget remaining for another round, stopping is appropriate."
